---
title: Shepherds Pie
source: https://www.thewholesomedish.com/the-best-classic-shepherds-pie/#recipe
servings: 6
---

Add {olive oil: 2tbsp} to a large skillet and place it over medium-high heat for 2 minutes.
Add {yellow onion 'chopped': 2cup}. Cook 5 minutes, stirring occasionally.

Add {ground beef '90% lean': 500gr} to the skillet and break it apart with a wooden spoon.
Add the {parsley 'dried': 2tsp}, {rosemay 'dried': 1tsp}, {thyme 'dried': 1tsp}, {salt: 0.5tsp} and {black pepper: 0.5tsp}.
Stir well. Cook for 6~8 minutes, until the meat is browned, stirring occasionally.

Add {worcestershire sauce: 1tbsp} and {garlic 'minced': 2}. Stir to combine. Cook for 1 minute.

Add {flour: 2tbsp} and {tomato paste: 2tbsp}. Stir until well incorporated and no clumps of tomato paste remain.

Add {beef broth: 1cup}, {frozen peas: 0.5cup} {frozen carrots: 0.5cup}, and {frozen corn: 0.5cup}. Bring the liquid
to a boil then reduce to simmer. Simmer for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally.

Set the meat mixture aside. Preheat the oven to 400F.

Place {potatoes 'peeled and cut into 1 inch cube': 1kg} in a large pot. Cover the potatoes with water. Bring the water to a boil.
Reduce to a simmer. Cook until potatoes are fork tender, 10~15 minutes.

Drain the potatoes in a colander. Return the potatoes to the hot pot.
Let the potatoes rest in the hot pot for 1 minute to evaporate any remaining liquid.

Add {butter 'unsalted': 8tbsp}, half & half, {garlic powder: 0.5tsp}, {salt: 0.5tsp}, and {black pepper: 0.25tsp}.
Mash the potatoes and stir until all the ingredients are mixed together.

Pour the meat mixture into a 9x9 (or 7x11) inch baking dish.
Spread it out into an even layer. 
Spoon the mashed potatoes on top of the meat. Carefully spread into an even layer.

If the baking dish looks very full, place it on a rimmed baking sheet so that the filling doesn’t bubble over into your oven.
Bake uncovered for 25-30 minutes.** Cool for 15 minutes before serving.


